  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"256\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c460ebbe-546c-4fa1-8b09-72bb7f5ab5cd-image.png\" width=\"517\" /></p><p>The&nbsp;polymers&nbsp;made by&nbsp;addition polymerisation&nbsp;from two different monomers are termed as copolymers, e.g.,&nbsp;Buna-S,&nbsp;Buna-N, etc.</p><p>Bakelite&nbsp;is a&nbsp;condensation polymer&nbsp;of formaldehyde and phenol . In practice, the phenol and formaldehyde are first polymerized to a small extent by using the proper choice of catalyst and temperature.</p><p>Nylon is also condensation polymer.</p>",
